WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.998
HTTP is a request-response protocol with methods, headers, status codes, and representations.

00:00:07.148 --> 00:00:12.044
A REST-style API exposes resources and uses method semantics consistently.

00:00:12.194 --> 00:00:16.343
GET should be safe; POST commonly creates or executes an operation.

00:00:16.493 --> 00:00:21.688
Idempotence means repeated equivalent requests have the same intended effect, not necessarily

00:00:21.688 --> 00:00:23.420
the same response bytes.

00:00:23.570 --> 00:00:31.128
Define the contract before implementation: path, method, input schema, authentication, pagination, success

00:00:31.128 --> 00:00:33.017
responses, and errors.

00:00:33.167 --> 00:00:38.488
Distinguish 400 for invalid input, 404 for missing accessible resources, 409 for

00:00:38.488 --> 00:00:43.808
a state conflict, and 202 for accepted work whose outcome is pending.

00:00:43.958 --> 00:00:47.101
A timeout does not tell the client whether the server committed.

00:00:47.251 --> 00:00:52.167
The inventory API accepts POST /reservations with an Idempotency-Key and a product

00:00:52.167 --> 00:00:52.986
and quantity.

00:00:53.136 --> 00:00:57.424
The orders API returns a PENDING order with 202 when inventory’s outcome

00:00:57.424 --> 00:00:58.138
is unknown.

00:00:58.288 --> 00:01:01.269
A repeated logical checkout reuses the same key.

00:01:01.419 --> 00:01:06.111
The provided contract files describe these semantics for the local learning services.

00:01:06.261 --> 00:01:12.768
Write an API contract for cancelling an order, including already-cancelled, already-shipped, unknown-order,

00:01:12.768 --> 00:01:14.395
and unauthorized cases.

00:01:14.545 --> 00:01:17.409
Decide which responses may safely be retried.

00:01:17.559 --> 00:01:22.871
Make cancellation idempotent for the same intent, validate ownership, and return a

00:01:22.871 --> 00:01:25.528
conflict when shipment makes cancellation impossible.

00:01:25.678 --> 00:01:30.063
Define whether inaccessible and absent resources share a 404 response.

00:01:30.213 --> 00:01:34.563
A client should preserve the original logical request identity on retries.

00:01:34.713 --> 00:01:35.385
Question.

00:01:35.535 --> 00:01:39.259
Is HTTP 200 proof that the business task succeeded?

00:01:39.409 --> 00:01:39.985
Answer.

00:01:40.135 --> 00:01:44.535
Only if the documented response semantics say so; a response may contain

00:01:44.535 --> 00:01:46.735
a pending or rejected business state.

00:01:46.885 --> 00:01:47.556
Question.

00:01:47.706 --> 00:01:49.776
What does a client timeout imply?

00:01:49.926 --> 00:01:50.502
Answer.

00:01:50.652 --> 00:01:51.883
The result is unknown.

00:01:52.033 --> 00:01:54.867
The server may have committed before the connection failed.
